  "goodToKnow": "Die Residenz is the residence of a ruler, a bishop or an ambassador, usually a palace: die Würzburger Residenz (a UNESCO World Heritage site with a famous staircase ceiling by Tiepolo), die Münchner Residenz of the Bavarian kings. Germany was once a patchwork of small states, so many towns are former Residenzstädte, with palaces and theatres to show for it. Residieren means to reside, often grandly. Plural: die Residenzen."
